  "findings": [
    "Only newly scheduled marked envelopes use the strict occurrence, parent, generation and source-state validator; legacy user/notification/recovery paths retain their existing contracts.",
    "The actual scheduler creates a foreground-service PendingIntent only for FIRED and an existing-receiver PendingIntent for other supported states. Both new types and the exact legacy service identity are cancelled on reschedule/cancel.",
    "The Service checks the actual row before the handler and the same occurrence/state after it; a void handler return cannot authorize starting sound.",
    "A matching already-current FIRED occurrence is not started twice. Persisted FIRED without a current service can resume; expired occurrences route through the existing recovery method.",
    "Rejected/missing/changed instances call stopSelf(startId) only when no current alarm exists, preserving another active alarm.",
    "Receiver cleanup attempts PendingResult.finish and wakelock release on handler failure; typed/catchall and register joins still require actual ART validation.",
    "The host VM executes reviewed instruction paths but explicitly doubles three App delegates: handleIntent, registerInstance and startAlarm, in addition to Android API boundaries. Its53 checks are not actual Provider, notification, foreground service or alarm execution."
  ],
